+Feature: LocalStorage persistence
+  As a user
+  I want my todos to survive page reloads
+  So that I don't lose my work
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  Scenario: Todos persist after page reload
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 2 items
+    And the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed state persists after page reload
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the page is reloaded
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+  Scenario: Edited title persists after page reload
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "Buy eggs"
+    And the user presses Enter on the edit input
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Deleted todo stays deleted after page reload
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user clicks the first todo destroy button
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: localStorage key uses the correct format
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage contains a key "todos-todomvc"
+
+  Scenario: localStorage value contains an array of todo objects
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then localStorage["todos-todomvc"] is a JSON array
+    And each todo has keys "id", "title", "completed"
+
+  Scenario: Empty list after all todos are deleted persists as empty
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the first todo destroy button
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
