+Feature: Routing and filtering
+  As a user
+  I want to filter my todo list by All, Active, or Completed
+  So that I can focus on the subset of todos I care about
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # ── Route defaults ──
+
+  Scenario: Default route shows all todos
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/"
+    Then the todo list shows 2 items
+
+  Scenario: Hash change to #/active shows only active todos
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Hash change to #/completed shows only completed todos
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/completed"
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is completed
+
+  # ── Filter link highlighting ──
+
+  Scenario: All link is selected on #/
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/"
+    Then the filter link "All" is selected
+    And the filter link "Active" is not selected
+    And the filter link "Completed" is not selected
+
+  Scenario: Active link is selected on #/active
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    Then the filter link "Active" is selected
+    And the filter link "All" is not selected
+    And the filter link "Completed" is not selected
+
+  Scenario: Completed link is selected on #/completed
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/completed"
+    Then the filter link "Completed" is selected
+    And the filter link "All" is not selected
+    And the filter link "Active" is not selected
+
+  # ── Filtering interaction ──
+
+  Scenario: Completing a todo hides it in Active filter
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+
+  Scenario: Uncompleting a todo hides it in Completed filter
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/completed"
+    And the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the todo list shows 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Adding a todo while on Active filter shows it
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And the user types "Walk dog" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Deleting a todo while filtered updates the list
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And the user clicks the first todo destroy button
+    Then the todo list shows 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+  # ── Route persistence ──
+
+  Scenario: Active filter persists across page reload
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the route is "#/active"
+    And the page is reloaded
+    Then the filter link "Active" is selected
+    And the todo list shows 1 item
diff --git a/features/todos.feature b/features/todos.feature
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..e075843
--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/todos.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@
+Feature: Todo CRUD
+  As a user
+  I want to create, complete, edit, and delete todos
+  So that I can manage my task list
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # ── Adding ──
+
+  Scenario: Adding a todo via Enter
+    Given the new-todo input is focused
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+    And the new-todo input is empty
+
+  Scenario: Trims whitespace from new todo titles
+    When the user types "  Buy milk  " and presses Enter
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Does not create a todo from blank input
+    When the user types "   " and presses Enter
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: New-todo input is focused on page load
+    Then the new-todo input is focused
+
+  # ── Completing ──
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox completes a todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is completed
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the checkbox again uncompletes a todo
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Completed todo has the completed class
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the first todo has class "completed"
+
+  # ── Mark all ──
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all completes every todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox on
+    Then every todo is completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all uncompletes every todo
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user toggles the toggle-all checkbox on
+    Then every todo is not completed
+    And the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all becomes checked when all todos are completed individually
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    And the user toggles the second todo checkbox
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is checked
+
+  Scenario: Toggle-all becomes unchecked when a todo is uncompleted
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
+
+  # ── Editing ──
+
+  Scenario: Double-clicking a label enters editing mode
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    Then the first todo has class "editing"
+    And the first todo edit input has value "Buy milk"
+    And the first todo edit input is focused
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on Enter
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "Buy eggs"
+    And the user presses Enter on the edit input
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+    And the first todo does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Editing saves on blur
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "Buy eggs"
+    And the edit input loses focus
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Editing with empty text destroys the todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to ""
+    And the user presses Enter on the edit input
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Editing with blank-only text destroys the todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "   "
+    And the user presses Enter on the edit input
+    Then the todo list contains 0 items
+
+  Scenario: Escape discards editing changes
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "Buy eggs"
+    And the user presses Escape on the edit input
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy milk" and is not completed
+    And the first todo does not have class "editing"
+
+  Scenario: Trims whitespace during edit save
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user double-clicks the first todo label
+    And the first todo edit input is changed to "  Buy eggs  "
+    And the user presses Enter on the edit input
+    Then the first todo has title "Buy eggs" and is not completed
+
+  # ── Deleting ──
+
+  Scenario: Clicking the destroy button removes a todo
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user clicks the first todo destroy button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+  # ── Clear completed ──
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed removes all completed todos
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    And a completed todo "Read book"
+    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the todo list contains 1 item
+    And the first todo has title "Walk dog" and is not completed
+
+  Scenario: Clear completed resets the toggle-all checkbox
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the toggle-all checkbox is not checked
diff --git a/features/visibility.feature b/features/visibility.feature
new file mode 100644
