--- /dev/null
+++ b/features/visibility.feature
@@ -0,0 +1,69 @@
+Feature: Section visibility and counter
+  As a user
+  I want the app to show and hide sections appropriately
+  So that I see only what is relevant to the current state
+
+  Background:
+    Given the app is loaded
+
+  # ── Empty state ──
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer are hidden when there are no todos
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer appear after adding a todo
+    When the user types "Buy milk" and presses Enter
+    Then the main section is visible
+    And the footer section is visible
+
+  Scenario: Main and footer disappear when all todos are deleted
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the first todo destroy button
+    Then the main section is hidden
+    And the footer section is hidden
+
+  # ── Counter ──
+
+  Scenario: Counter shows the number of active todos
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    Then the counter text is "2 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter counts only active (not completed) todos
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a completed todo "Walk dog"
+    Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses singular form for one item
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter uses plural form for zero items
+    Then the counter text is "0 items left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a todo is completed
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    And a todo "Walk dog"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+  Scenario: Counter updates when a completed todo is uncompleted
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user toggles the first todo checkbox
+    Then the counter text is "1 item left"
+
+  # ── Clear completed visibility ──
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button is hidden when no todos are completed
+    Given a todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button is visible when a todo is completed
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    Then the clear-completed button is visible
+
+  Scenario: Clear-completed button hides after all completed todos are removed
+    Given a completed todo "Buy milk"
+    When the user clicks the clear-completed button
+    Then the clear-completed button is hidden
